# Secrets

Every credential this project touches, and where it lives.
{% if use_terraform %}

## Local: Terraform variables

Terraform supports several ways to provide variables; this project uses `*.tfvars` files locally and `TF_VAR_*` environment variables in CI (see below). Each environment has its own file under `terraform/environments/<env>/`, gitignored and created from the committed `.example`:

```shell
{% if use_staging_environment %}
cp terraform/environments/staging/terraform.tfvars.example terraform/environments/staging/terraform.tfvars
{% endif %}
cp terraform/environments/production/terraform.tfvars.example terraform/environments/production/terraform.tfvars
```

| Variable               | Purpose                                                          |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `hcloud_token`          | Hetzner Cloud API token.                                          |
| `ssh_authorized_key`    | Public key installed on provisioned servers (see `task gen-ssh-key`). |
| `ssh_priv_key_file`     | Path to the matching private key, used to connect during provisioning. |
| `cloudflare_api_token`  | Cloudflare API token, for managing DNS/security settings.         |
| `cloudflare_zone_id`    | Cloudflare Zone ID for the managed domain.                        |

None of these are committed - only the `.example` files with placeholder values are.
{% endif %}
{% if ansible_enabled %}

## Local: Ansible Vault

Secrets consumed by the playbook live encrypted in each environment's `inventory/<env>/group_vars/all/vault.yml`, and **are** committed to git - only the vault password itself stays out of version control.

```shell
# once, shared across environments
openssl rand -base64 32 > ansible/.vault-pass

# per environment
cp ansible/inventory/{% if use_staging_environment %}staging{% else %}production{% endif %}/group_vars/all/vault.example.yml ansible/inventory/{% if use_staging_environment %}staging{% else %}production{% endif %}/group_vars/all/vault.yml
task ansible:vault-encrypt ENV={% if use_staging_environment %}staging{% else %}production{% endif %}
```

`.vault-pass` is gitignored. See `ansible/README.md` for the full vault workflow (`vault-edit`, `vault-view`, `vault-decrypt`).
{% endif %}

## CI: GitHub Actions secrets

Set under Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions:

| Secret Name              | Purpose                                                                                                                                                              | Required |
| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |
{% if use_terraform and terraform_backend == "tfc" %}
| `TF_API_TOKEN`           | API token for authenticating with Terraform Cloud. Generate one [here](https://app.terraform.io/app/{{ tfc_organization }}/settings/authentication-tokens).       | ✅        |
{% endif %}
{% if use_terraform and terraform_backend == "s3" %}
| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`      | AWS access key with read/write access to the `{{ terraform_s3_bucket }}` state bucket.                                                                             | ✅        |
| `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`  | Secret matching `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`.                                                                                                                                | ✅        |
{% endif %}
{% if use_terraform and terraform_backend != "local" %}
| `CF_API_TOKEN`           | API token for authenticating with Cloudflare, used by Terraform to manage Cloudflare resources.                                                                    | ✅        |
| `CF_ZONE_ID`             | Cloudflare Zone ID, specifying which domain or zone Terraform should manage.                                                                                       | ✅        |
| `HCLOUD_TOKEN`           | Hetzner Cloud API token, allowing Terraform to manage infrastructure in Hetzner Cloud.                                                                              | ✅        |
| `SSH_AUTHORIZED_KEY`     | Public SSH key used for provisioning and accessing cloud instances securely.                                                                                       | ✅        |
| `SSH_PRIVATE_KEY`        | Private key matching `SSH_AUTHORIZED_KEY`, used by CI (`terraform`{% if ansible_enabled %}, `provision`{% endif %}) to connect to provisioned servers.             | ✅        |
{% endif %}
{% if ansible_enabled %}
| `ANSIBLE_VAULT_PASSWORD` | Vault password, used to decrypt `vault.yml`. Required even on a fresh project - CI's syntax-check always passes `--vault-password-file`.                          | ✅        |
{% endif %}

No secrets are needed for the `docs` workflow - `deploy-pages`/`configure-pages` use the built-in `GITHUB_TOKEN` and OIDC.
{% if use_terraform %}
{% if terraform_backend == "local" %}

With the `local` backend, `terraform`'s plan/apply/drift jobs don't run in CI at all (state only exists on your machine) - only `lint` does, and it needs none of the secrets above. See [CI/CD](ci-cd.md).
{% elif use_staging_environment %}

These apply to both the `staging` and `production` environments alike - there's no per-environment secret, since the `apply` jobs' [GitHub Environment](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/deployment/targeting-different-environments/using-environments-for-deployment) mapping is what separates them (see [CI/CD](ci-cd.md)).
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
